---
const points = [
  ["01", "Schemas reflect intent, not code", "A contract can describe a type change without showing which downstream code reads that value."],
  ["02", "Distributed codebases hide callers", "When consumers live across repositories, the caller list is not reliably held in memory."],
  ["03", "Review needs evidence", "A useful review names the affected path and keeps uncertainty visible when tracing cannot establish an answer."]
];
---
<section class="section problem">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">The problem space</span>
      <h2>Shared APIs cross boundaries that unit tests do not see.</h2>
      <p>A pull request can be green in the provider repository while downstream callers still need review.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="points">{points.map(([number, title, copy]) => <article><span class="number">{number}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></article>)}</div>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .problem { background: var(--color-background); }
  .points { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--space-8); margin-top: var(--space-12); }
  article { border-top: 2px solid var(--color-navy); padding-top: var(--space-4); }
  .number { color: var(--color-primary); font: 700 var(--text-xs)/1 var(--font-mono); }
  h3 { margin: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-2); color: var(--color-navy); font-size: var(--text-xl); }
  article p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-secondary); line-height: var(--leading-copy); }
  @media (max-width: 48rem) { .points { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-6); } }
</style>
